med regional chapters in the mia and  aipac  and functional chapters that are  organizational or team-based  like women of core infrastructure we tap  into each other's platforms  and connect as a stronger global network  of women and allies  we also want to recognize that community  is inside and outside  there needs to be a balance between the  work that we do here at google  and how we share and invite other  leaders to join us in that mission  last year we partnered with the kellogg  school of management to launch a global  speaker series  where we brought their professors who  are experts in the field  to deliver sprints of professional  development topics  we had about 200 members attend each  talk and it sparked  internal dialogue with one another in  addition to offering  external networking opportunities  our third and last pillar is empower and  develop  this is centered on providing  opportunities for professional  development and training  as well as supporting the promotion of  women to leadership positions  it is so important to create a culture  of celebration and recognition for the  growth and accomplishments of what we do  our members every day go well beyond  just our teams or our customers  we have an opportunity to share our  knowledge learn from one another  and create stronger impact when we act  together so every quarter we highlight  the awesome work happening around the  world in a newsletter  and encourage recognition across teams  into our senior leadership  this is another place where executive  sponsorship really comes in  we want to lift amplify and build trust  across google cloud  if there's one lesson we've picked up  since 2014 it's that we're always  learning  we're always growing and it never hurts  to have some fun along the way  looking ahead while we're all navigating  the remote working situation  we especially want to lean into  listening to our community  in march we took steps to re-evaluate  all of our 2020 programming  t